final_image_tex = SubResource("Resource_vb4tv")
province = 55
blurb = "Depicts a group of figures buffeted by a sudden gust of wind on an open marsh road in Suruga province (present-day central Shizuoka Prefecture).

A traveling hat is swept off a man's head, and a stream of papers (likely tissues) whirls away from a woman's backpack, as her face is covered by a wind-tossed cloth.

Mount Fuji is composed of a simple unfinished contour line, letting the focus remain on the dramatic foreground.

This design is an example of Hokusai's theme of natural forces overpowering humans, most famously expressed in the Great Wave Off Kanagawa.

The scene is set in Ejiri, a station on the Tōkaidō, which was located on the west side of the port of Shimizu in Suruga Bay, near modern-day Shimizu City."
metadata/_custom_type_script = "uid://6kpsqyb2pk7a"
